<article class="env-lemma" id="0GUG">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0GUG">Lemma <span data-tag="0GUG">42.47.3</span>.</a> In Lemma <a href="/tag/0F9H" data-tag="0F9H">42.47.1</a> let $X' \to X$ be a morphism which is locally of finite type. Denote $X' = X'_1 \cup X'_2$ and $E'_2 \in D(\mathcal{O}_{X'_2})$ the pullbacks to $X'$. Then the class $P'_ p(E_2')$, resp. $c'_ p(E_2')$ in $A^ p(X_2' \to X')$ constructed in Lemma <a href="/tag/0F9H" data-tag="0F9H">42.47.1</a> using $X' = X'_1 \cup X'_2$ and $E_2'$ is the restriction (Remark <a href="/tag/0F9Z" data-tag="0F9Z">42.33.5</a>) of the class $P'_ p(E_2)$, resp. $c'_ p(E_2)$ in $A^ p(X_2 \to X)$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Immediate from the characterization of these classes in Lemma <a href="/tag/0F9H" data-tag="0F9H">42.47.1</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>